-bit size and time fields, specifically called ","type":"text"},{"code":"_stat32()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Microsoft’s compiler, by default struct stat means one with","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"64-bit time fields while in MinGW struct stat is the legacy one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with 32-bit fields. To hopefully clear up this messs, the gstdio.h","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"header defines a type ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/StatBuf","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" which is the appropriate struct type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"depending on the platform and\/or compiler being used. On POSIX it","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is just struct stat, but note that even on POSIX platforms, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"might be a macro.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See your C library manual for more details about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/stat(filename:buf:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A wrapper for the POSIX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat()"},{"text":" function. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"returns information about a file. On Windows the ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the C library checks only the FAT-style READONLY attribute and does","typ